cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the following publications."
type: software
title: "WRF-WAVE: the Weather Research and Forecasting model with a moving bottom boundary and wave phase-resolved capability"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/windscape-model/WRF-WAVE"
abstract: >-
  WRF-WAVE adds a phase-resolved, moving ocean-surface-wave capability to the
  Weather Research and Forecasting (WRF) Model, version 3.8.1. The moving-wave
  capability is implemented in the ARW (dyn_em) dynamical core as a prescribed
  moving lower boundary that represents propagating surface waves. This enables
  high-fidelity large-eddy simulation (LES) of airflow over moving surface waves.
keywords:
  - WRF
  - large-eddy simulation
  - ocean surface waves
  - moving wave
  - wind-wave interaction
  - atmospheric boundary layer
